# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in every working tree.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF, and a CRLF
# shebang is not executable on Linux: the kernel reads the interpreter as
# "bash\r" and the script fails with
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# These run on the Ubuntu build and flash rigs, and copies made from a Windows
# checkout reached christielab10 that way. Scoped to scripts, so no other file
# is renormalised.
*.sh text eol=lf
tools/reachaq-firmware text eol=lf
tools/reachaq-update text eol=lf
